-- title:
--   Schauder–Tychonoff fixed points in products of real lines
-- statement:
--   Let $I$ be an arbitrary index set and equip $\mathbb R^I$ with its product topology. Every continuous self-map $f:K\to K$ of a nonempty compact convex set $K\subseteq\mathbb R^I$ has a fixed point:
--
--   $$\exists x\in K,\qquad f(x)=x.$$
--
--   No finite-dimensionality assumption is imposed on the product.
-- source:
